## Zone-based firewall

Enable zone-based firewall **manually in the UniFi Network UI** before managing:

- [`unifi_firewall_zone`](docs/resources/firewall_zone)
- [`unifi_firewall_policy`](docs/resources/firewall_policy)
- [`unifi_firewall_policy_ordering`](docs/resources/firewall_policy_ordering)

Otherwise the controller returns `api.firewall.zone-based-firewall-not-configured`.

### Known controller quirks

- Treat the system **Internal** zone as read-only. Moving networks with `zone_id` works; explicit updates to built-in zone membership may be rejected.
- Set `allow_return_traffic` **explicitly** on every `ALLOW` policy. Some builds reject filtered `ALLOW` rules when the field is omitted, even if you intend `false`.
- `protocol_filter = { type = "NAMED_PROTOCOL" }` is currently only reliable for `ICMP`. For TCP/UDP services prefer `protocol_filter = { type = "PRESET", preset_name = "TCP_UDP" }` plus a nested destination `port_filter`.
- Prefer importing or aligning `unifi_firewall_policy_ordering` **after** policies exist.
- Legacy UI-created policies may be hard to import if list endpoints omit stable IDs.

Full write-up: [Zone-based firewall](docs/guides/zone-based-firewall).

## WiFi notes

- After WiFi (and some other) changes, UniFi may stop answering the API for minutes while devices reprovision — raise `request_timeout_seconds` (for example `300`) if you see deadline errors mid-apply.
- Enterprise security references an existing RADIUS profile via [`data.unifi_radius_profile`](docs/data-sources/radius_profile) (Integration API is read-only for profiles).
- WPA2 PPSK and Enterprise are separate modes; do not assume they coexist on one broadcast.
- UniFi responses may omit PPSK passphrases; known state secrets are preserved on refresh, but **imported** PPSK broadcasts need passphrases supplied in configuration.
- `IOT_OPTIMIZED` broadcasts only allow a subset of security modes; unsupported combinations are rejected or warned at plan time (see changelog / resource docs).

